# Server runtime (joinUp)

## Rate limiter must not 429 health checks or Socket.IO
- A global Express limiter counting `/api/health` (Coolify probes) or `/api/socket` (Engine.IO
  polling) causes false 429s.
  Fix: `server/middleware/rateLimit.js` must skip Jest (`NODE_ENV=test` / `JEST_WORKER_ID`),
  `OPTIONS`, `/api/health`, and `/api/socket`. Do not count Engine.IO polling or health probes.

## Batch socket permission lookups
- `joinChats` must batch `ChatParticipant` lookups with `chatId: { in: ids }`
  (`checkChatPermissionsBatch`). Never loop `checkChatPermission` / `findFirst` per room — homepage
  reload was ~60 identical lookups.
- Game list endpoints use `SEARCH_GAME_SELECT` (no nested `user`); keep full
  `include: { user: true }` for `getGameById` only.

## Multi-instance (Redis) rules
- Multi-instance API (Redis, all opt-in flags): the adapter alone is not enough. (1) Bridged events (`joinup:socket_events`, `moderation_events`) must be applied with `io.local`, or each of N instances re-broadcasts to the cluster and clients get N copies. (2) `io.sockets.adapter.rooms`/`io.sockets.sockets` are node-local; use `utils/socketPresence`. (3) The adapter fires `pubClient.publish()` un-awaited, so a down Redis becomes unhandled rejections unless `socket/adapter.js` `guardPublish` + fail-fast pub / queueing sub clients (`lib/redis.js createAdapterClients`) are kept. (4) Jobs run on one process only: `JOBS_LEADER_LOCK=redis` elects it; standbys must never re-publish scheduler signals (`gameScheduler.handleSignal`). Details: `server/docs/agents/realtime_rules.md` §4-5.
- Redis features are opt-in flags with in-memory defaults (`SOCKET_ADAPTER`, `RATE_LIMIT_STORE`,
  `CHAT_RATE_STORE`, `CHAT_DEDUPE_STORE`, `JOBS_LEADER_LOCK`); every one must fail open when Redis is
  down. New Redis clients come from `lib/redis.js` (retry forever, capped backoff) — never copy the
  old `retryStrategy: times > 3 → null`, which permanently ends cross-node delivery after one blip.
- Cross-user socket state (online, delivered) comes from `utils/socketPresence` (`fetchSockets`),
  never from `io.sockets.adapter.rooms` / `io.sockets.sockets` (node-local).
- Redis-originated socket events that every instance applies (`joinup:socket_events`,
  `moderation_events`) use `io.local`, otherwise the adapter multiplies them N-fold.
- Tests that need Redis use `TEST_REDIS_URL` (never `REDIS_URL`, which makes moderationService
  connect) via `describeRedis` in `tests/helpers/redisTest.js`; close every socket/io/redis client.

## Worker / API process split
- A dedicated jobs process is `node worker.js` (`RUN_HTTP_SERVER=false`). The web API sitting next to
  it must set `RUN_BACKGROUND_JOBS=false` (see `server-invariants.mdc`) unless `JOBS_LEADER_LOCK=redis`
  is on, in which case `worker.js` and API instances compete for the lock. Worker socket emits go
  through Redis `joinup:socket_events`.
